          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Are Light-Cure Tooth-Coloured Fillings?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            When food and bacteria wear a tiny hole (cavity) into a tooth, treating it early prevents the decay from reaching the inner nerve. A tooth-coloured composite filling replaces the decayed portion using a smooth resin matched to your natural enamel shade and hardened instantly with a safe blue curing light—leaving no dark metallic spot when you smile or speak.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Signs You May Need a Filling</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>Black or brown spots on the chewing grooves or between teeth.</li>
            <li>Food getting stuck repeatedly in the same tooth gap.</li>
            <li>Mild twinge when eating sweets or drinking cold water.</li>
            <li>A small chipped edge on a front or back tooth.</li>
            <li>A loose, cracked, or worn-out older dental filling.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Step-by-Step Procedure</h2>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12 items-center">
            <div class="sm:col-span-4 aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden img-frame">
              <img src="/images/thumbs/dental-chair-treatment-room-jaipur.webp" alt="Modern treatment chair with light-cure unit at Shanti Dental Hospital Jaipur" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" width="640" height="480" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
            </div>
            <div class="sm:col-span-8 p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[#2A9D8F]">Natural Shade &amp; Instant Cure</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Single-Visit Cavity Protection</h3>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">Treating shallow decay early with light-cure composite takes 20–30 minutes in one visit and prevents deeper infection.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ol class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base text-slate-700 list-decimal pl-5">
            <li><strong>Examination &amp; Shade Match:</strong> Dr. Shubham Gupta checks how deep the cavity is and picks the composite shade matching your tooth.</li>
            <li><strong>Gentle Decay Cleaning:</strong> Softened decay is cleared gently (with local numbing if the cavity is deep).</li>
            <li><strong>Bonding &amp; Layering:</strong> Tooth-coloured resin is placed in thin layers and hardened immediately with a light-cure unit.</li>
            <li><strong>Bite Check &amp; Polish:</strong> The filling is shaped to match your natural bite and polished smooth.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
